M.1  THE JOINT STRUCTURE IS READ FROM THE BOUNDARIES ALONE
     for each pair, the shared contents and the orientations their
     excluded sectors demand there.  No partial orientation is
     formed and the envelope is not touched.

      Instance 1: 43 boundaries, 289 opposed pairs, sharing counts {delta=1: 461, delta=2: 156, delta=3: 7}
    PASS  Instance 1: the relations are read from the symbols of each pair, 289 of them   [at most C(m,2) = 903]
    PASS  Instance 1: every relation names only contents both boundaries hold   [a relation outside the shared support would not be a relation of the pair]
      Instance 2: 51 boundaries, 374 opposed pairs, sharing counts {delta=1: 630, delta=2: 150, delta=3: 4}
    PASS  Instance 2: the relations are read from the symbols of each pair, 374 of them   [at most C(m,2) = 1275]
    PASS  Instance 2: every relation names only contents both boundaries hold   [a relation outside the shared support would not be a relation of the pair]

    PASS  reading the relations requires no address and no depth   [joint_relations takes the boundaries and nothing else; it forms no orientation, enters no stratum and touches no address]

M.2  ON THE FAMILY WHERE RESOLUTION IS PROVABLY EXPONENTIAL
     Tseitin formulas over 3-regular graphs, unsatisfiable, width 3
     with no encoding step.  The boundaries hold the joint structure;
     a traversal re-encounters it once per region it enters.

          instance     n     m   stored  relations   traversal    ratio
         tseitin-8    12    32      109         96          32       --
        tseitin-10    15    40      136        120          64    1.25x
        tseitin-12    18    48      163        144         128    1.20x
        tseitin-14    21    56      190        168         256    1.17x
        tseitin-16    24    64      217        192         512    1.14x
        tseitin-18    27    72      244        216       1,024    1.12x
        tseitin-20    30    80      271        240       2,048    1.11x
        tseitin-22    33    88      298        264       4,096    1.10x
        tseitin-24    36    96      325        288       8,192    1.09x
        tseitin-26    39   104      352        312      16,384    1.08x

    PASS  the relations held in the boundaries grow by a constant increment   [increment 24 at every step, relations 96 to 312]
    PASS  the relations are linear in the number of boundaries   [relations/m from 3.00 to 3.00]
    PASS  a traversal's encounters with the same structure double at every step   [32 to 16,384, ratio 2.00 throughout]
    PASS  at the largest size the boundaries hold the structure in a small fraction of what a traversal meets   [312 relations against 16,384 encounters]

M.3  THE RELATIONS ARE COMPLETE AND WITNESSED
     a pair can close a region exactly when its excluded sectors
     demand opposite orientations on a content they share.  For
     every pair, the static read is checked against a constructed
     partial orientation at which both boundaries stand forcing.

    PASS  Instance 1: every relation read from the boundaries is witnessed by a partial orientation at which the pair closes   289/289
    PASS  Instance 2: every relation read from the boundaries is witnessed by a partial orientation at which the pair closes   374/374
    PASS  tseitin-8: every relation read from the boundaries is witnessed by a partial orientation at which the pair closes   96/96
    PASS  tseitin-10: every relation read from the boundaries is witnessed by a partial orientation at which the pair closes   120/120
    PASS  tseitin-12: every relation read from the boundaries is witnessed by a partial orientation at which the pair closes   144/144
    PASS  tseitin-14: every relation read from the boundaries is witnessed by a partial orientation at which the pair closes   168/168
    PASS  Instance 1: no pair outside the relations can demand opposite orientations on a shared content   [the read is exhaustive over pairs, so a closing pair cannot be missed]
    PASS  Instance 2: no pair outside the relations can demand opposite orientations on a shared content   [the read is exhaustive over pairs, so a closing pair cannot be missed]
    PASS  tseitin-8: no pair outside the relations can demand opposite orientations on a shared content   [the read is exhaustive over pairs, so a closing pair cannot be missed]
    PASS  tseitin-10: no pair outside the relations can demand opposite orientations on a shared content   [the read is exhaustive over pairs, so a closing pair cannot be missed]

    PASS  the relation is a fact about a pair of boundaries, not about a depth   [joint_relations consults only the mask and value of each pair; the witness is constructed afterwards to confirm the condition, and is no part of the read]

